Easnap @EASNAP_VERSION_TEXT@ | Windows x64
==================================

Screenshots with annotations, scrolling screenshots, MP4 recording and GIF
export. Needs Windows 10 version 2004 (build 19041) or later, 64-bit.

START
Extract the entire ZIP to a folder you can write to. Open bin\Easnap.exe.
Easnap appears in the notification area; use its menu or press Ctrl+Shift+A
to start a capture. The shortcut, the language and the folders are under
Settings in that menu.

Keep Easnap.exe and EasnapPreviewHost.exe together in the bin folder. The
preview helper is launched by Easnap; do not start it separately. No separate
Visual C++ runtime is needed. Recording needs the Windows media components;
on an N edition of Windows, install the Media Feature Pack for it. The same
release also offers a per-user installer if you prefer a Start menu entry.

USE
Select a region, then take a screenshot, a scrolling screenshot or start an
MP4/GIF recording. Annotate screenshots, or adjust a recording's start and end
in the trim window. Use Save or Copy to publish the result. GIF export does
not contain audio.

UPDATE OR REMOVE
Exit Easnap from the notification-area menu first. To update, extract the new
release into a new folder and start Easnap from there; never mix the two
executables of different releases. To remove the application, delete its
extracted folder.

Settings, the log, crash reports and temporary recordings are stored under
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Easnap, separate from this portable folder. Nothing in it is
sent anywhere. A recording you had not saved when Easnap ended is kept there
and offered at the next start; save or delete it before removing that data.
Copied recording files can remain there while the clipboard still refers to
them.

RELEASE NOTES AND SUPPORT
